<title>USA: TABLE-New York Times Co Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-New York Times Co Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second  Quarter	Six Months</p>
<p>				  1997     1996*	1997     1996*</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p>  Advertising	    $504,996 $449,685   $981,544  $881,302</p>
<p>  Circulation	     169,132  163,363    337,686   325,919</p>
<p>  Other			47,819   36,458     95,178    69,860</p>
<p>   Total		    721,947  649,506  1,414,408 1,277,081</p>
<p> Costs and Expenses     594,598  566,986  1,185,804 1,133,938</p>
<p> Operating Profit	 127,349   82,520    228,604   143,143</p>
<p> Income - Joint Ventures  3,052    2,210	4,367     6,892</p>
<p> Net Gain on Disposition     --    7,751	   --     7,751</p>
<p> Net Income		  84,949   46,812    136,788    79,526</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs **	  99,835   97,755    100,450    97,703</p>
<p> EPS **			  0.85     0.48	 1.36	0.81</p>
<p>(Dollars and shares in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				 ADJUSTED EPS CALCULATION</p>
<p>			  Quarter Ended June  Six Months Ended June</p>
<p>				1997	1996	  1997    1996</p>
<p> AS REPORTED EPS	  $0.85     $0.48	$1.36   $0.81</p>
<p>SPECIAL FACTORS:</p>
<p>   Add: Buyouts	     --	 0.02	 0.01    0.03</p>
<p>Subtract: Tax Adjustment (net APB 15</p>
<p>   Dilution* .01/shr    (0.18)	--	 (0.18)     --</p>
<p>   Gain Sale of 110 Fifth Ave --  (0.04)	 --    (0.04)</p>
<p> ADJUSTED EPS		 0.67	 0.46     1.19    0.80</p>
<p>Add: APB 15 Dilution* on</p>
<p>Net Income excluding</p>
<p>	Tax Adjustment	0.02	   --     0.04	--</p>
<p>Adjusted EPS without APB 15 Dilution</p>
<p> impact			0.69	 0.46     1.23    0.80</p>
<p>	 NOTE: * To be restated December 1997 to reflect</p>
<p>Statement of Financial Accounting Standards No. 128.</p>
<p>*  For comparability, certain 1996 amounts have been reclassified to conform with the 1997 presentation.</p>
<p>** The 1997 calculation reflects primary earnings per share including incremental shares associated with stock options in accordance with APB.</p>
<p>Analysts consensus for the quarter was $0.63 per share, according to First Call.</p>
<p>The special factors, exclusive of the tax adjustment, that affected the 1997 and 1996 reported results were a 1997 $2.5 million pre-tax charge ($.01 per share for the six months) for severance and related costs resulting from workforce reductions (&quot;buyouts&quot;).</p>
<p>In 1996, they included a $7.8 million pre-tax gain ($.04 per share for the second quarter and six months) from the sale of the 110 Fifth Avenue building and a $5.5 million pre-tax charge ($.02 per share for the second quarter and $.03 per share for the six months) for buyouts.</p>
